<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n75847" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐλο-μελίη</span></b> , ἡ, 
			Ion.
		 for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁλομέλεια</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>wholeness of limbs</i>: hence,
				<i>the general nature</i> of a thing, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περὶ ἀδένων οὐλομελίης</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>Art.</u>
					11
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Gland.</u>
				1
			</span></i> and <i><span class="en">
				7
			</span></i>, also cited by <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				<u>UP</u>
				1.8
			</span></i>: dat. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐλομελίῃ</span>, as
				Adv., 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καθόλου</span>
			, <i>upon the whole</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>; so <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατὰ οὐλομελίην</span>, opp.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατὰ μέρος</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Alim.</u>
				23
			</span></i>.—In <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Metaph.</u>
				1093b4
			</span></i>, codd. have <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῇ οὐλομελείᾳ τοῦ
				οὐρανοῦ</span> (leg. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁλομελείᾳ</span>, as in <i><span class="en">
				<u>Theol.Ar.</u>
				36
			</span></i>), <i>to the whole</i> celestial <i>system.</i></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
